; Stage 15 W3c fallout (cheader.md, "Unnamed `declare` parameters carry types").
;
; The interaction that made the parameter defect urgent: W3c gave an explicit
; `(declare …)` precedence over a C header's declaration of the same function,
; warning on a mismatch. With unnamed parameters defaulting to `i32`, a bare-list
; declaration that AGREED with the header rendered as `i64 (i32, i32, i32)`,
; overrode the header's correct `i64 (i32, i64, i32)`, and warned about a
; conflict that did not exist — and the wrong signature won.
;
; This declaration is character-for-character equivalent to <unistd.h>'s. It must
; produce no diagnostic at all, and exactly one, correct `declare`.
(import-use "unistd.h")
(declare lseek (i32 i64 i32):i64)

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
